---
import AgentPage from '../../components/home/AgentPage.astro';
---
<AgentPage
  name="Codex"
  logo="/assets/agents/codex.svg"
  headline="Codex, one per task."
  sub="Ouijit runs Codex in a worktree per task, shows when each one is thinking, and teaches it the ouijit command so it can drive the board."
  description="Run OpenAI Codex CLI in parallel with Ouijit: a git worktree and terminal per task, live status, and the ouijit CLI in its developer instructions."
  points={[
    [
      'Knows Ouijit',
      'The ouijit CLI reference is passed as developer instructions through a config override at launch, so Codex can create tasks, move cards and stage review comments without being told how.',
    ],
    [
      'Live status',
      "Codex's lifecycle hooks and its notify setting report when a turn starts and ends, passed as config overrides and pre-trusted so there is no hooks prompt. The card shows thinking or ready.",
    ],
    [
      'Sandboxed',
      "Codex's own sandbox covers the commands it runs. Ouijit's wraps the whole terminal, so anything Codex starts is inside too, and the same boundary applies to every agent in the project.",
    ],
  ]}
  startHook={'codex "$OUIJIT_TASK_DESCRIPTION"'}
  faqs={[
    [
      'Do I need to configure anything?',
      'No. Run codex in any Ouijit terminal. The status hooks and the CLI reference are injected per launch as config overrides. Outside Ouijit’s terminals, Codex is untouched.',
    ],
  ]}
/>
